Short Exam Definition

A Queue is a linear data structure that follows the FIFO principle, where insertion happens at the rear and deletion happens at the front.


Definition
A Queue is a data structure that follows the FIFO (First In, First Out) principle.

👉 The element that is inserted first will be removed first.

🔹 Real-Life Example
Think of a queue at a ticket counter 🎟️
The person who stands first gets the ticket first.
New people join at the back.


🔹 Queue Interface in Java

In Java, Queue is an interface in the java.util package.
Common classes that implement Queue:

LinkedList
PriorityQueue
ArrayDeque